      "writtenOn": "2026-07-17T16:58:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, [sys_heap_usable_size](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/zephyr/lib/heap/heap.c;l\u003d358?q\u003dthird_party%2Fzephyrproject%20sys_heap_usable_size\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch#:~:text\u003d357-,358,-359) does not handle a NULL pointer.\n\n```\nsize_t sys_heap_usable_size(struct sys_heap *heap, void *mem)\n{\n\tstruct z_heap *h \u003d heap-\u003eheap;\n\tchunkid_t c \u003d mem_to_chunkid(h, mem);\n\n\tif (SYS_HEAP_HARDENING_FULL) {\n\t\tverify_chunk_canary(h, c, mem);\n\t}\n\n\treturn chunk_usable_bytes(h, c) - mem_align_gap(h, mem);\n}\n```\n\nIt immediately passes the pointer (mem) to mem_to_chunkid() to calculate a chunk ID using pointer arithmetic without performing any NULL check first:\n\n```\nstatic chunkid_t mem_to_chunkid(struct z_heap *h, void *p)\n{\n\tuint8_t *mem \u003d p, *base \u003d (uint8_t *)chunk_buf(h);\n\treturn (mem - chunk_header_bytes(h) - base) / CHUNK_UNIT;\n}\n```\n\nPassing NULL to this function will cause underflow in the pointer subtraction and calculate an invalid, out-of-bounds chunkid_t, leading to memory corruption, assertions failing, or a kernel panic (especially when hardening is enabled).",
